From ba6162edacd5f8a5d6b87d5e6dcb856688c7c13d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 10:47:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sidebar): retain complete profile-scoped project
 membership [daveey]

The all-profile tree stamps individual rows, not project headers. Inferring
hidden membership from project.profile re-counted non-default-profile rows.
Carry complete id/profile membership from the profile reader through native
profile aggregation and gateway stamping/merging. Consult that membership
before either adding rows or synthesizing another folder node, retaining
owner/profile isolation even for identical durable ids.

RED: Python producer missing sessionMembership; Electron aggregate drops other
profile membership; renderer limited-preview regressions count 4 as 5 and
synthesize duplicate shells. GREEN: 83 sidebar/routing files, 1209 tests;
11 Python consumer files, 94 tests; full renderer typecheck and scripts/check.
